@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction
@cindex introduction

GNU Hyper Math (@code{libhypermath}) is a zero-dependency C++20 library
licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 or later (GPLv3+).
It unifies four foundational mathematical paradigms in a single coherent
architecture:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Hyper-Lattice Tensor Engine (@code{hyper_math::tensor})}:
64-byte cache-line aligned reference-counted @code{slab_buffer<T>},
rank-agnostic affine @code{lattice_descriptor}, lazily fused expression
templates, universal functions, Einstein summation (@code{einsum}), and
NumPy @code{.npy} binary serialization.
@item
@strong{Scientific Continuum (@code{hyper_math::scientific})}:
Dense and sparse linear algebra, arbitrary-length FFT (Cooley-Tukey +
Bluestein Chirp-Z), adaptive Gauss-Kronrod quadrature, Dormand-Prince
RK4(5) ODE solver, unconstrained and constrained optimization (BFGS,
L-BFGS-B, Nelder-Mead, Levenberg-Marquardt, Simplex LP), digital signal
filtering (@code{firwin}, @code{butter_lowpass_ba}, @code{filtfilt},
@code{welch}), spatial @math{k}-d trees, clustering, KDE, and PCA.
@item
@strong{Dual-Bitmask Columnar Engine (@code{hyper_math::tabular})}:
64-bit word @code{validity_bitmap} using hardware @code{std::popcount},
hash-indexed @code{index_axis}, @code{series} and @code{data_frame} with
multi-column and @code{asof} joins, pivot, melt, crosstab, ISO-8601
@code{.dt} accessors, and CSV / NDJSON / @code{.hmb} I/O.
@item
@strong{Lazy Relational Query Optimizer (@code{hyper_math::tabular::lazy_frame})}:
Declarative expression AST (@code{col}, @code{lit}, @code{when}, @code{over})
with algebraic constant folding, filter fusion, predicate pushdown, dead
column elimination, and projection pushdown.
@end itemize

@node Tensor Engine
@chapter Tensor Engine
@cindex tensor engine
@cindex nd_tensor

Include @code{<hyper_math/hyper_math.hpp>} and use namespace
@code{hyper_math::tensor}. Key facilities include:
@itemize @bullet
@item Creation: @code{zeros}, @code{ones}, @code{full}, @code{arange},
@code{linspace}, @code{logspace}, @code{eye}, @code{diag}, @code{meshgrid}.
@item Manipulation: @code{slice}, @code{transpose}, @code{reshape},
@code{concatenate}, @code{stack}, @code{column_stack}, @code{split},
@code{array_split}, @code{pad}, @code{roll}, @code{rot90}, @code{save_npy},
@code{load_npy}.
@item Contractions & Reductions: @code{matmul}, @code{dot}, @code{outer},
@code{kron}, @code{tensordot}, @code{einsum}, @code{sum}, @code{mean},
@code{var}, @code{std_dev}, @code{nansum}, @code{nanmean}, @code{nanstd}.
@end itemize

@node Scientific Continuum
@chapter Scientific Continuum
@cindex scientific continuum

The @code{hyper_math::scientific} namespace provides eleven submodules:
@code{linalg} (LU, LDL, QR, QZ, SVD, Schur, Sylvester/Lyapunov/Riccati,
matrix functions), @code{fft} (1D/2D/N-D FFT, DCT, DST, Fast Hankel Transform),
@code{integrate} (Gauss-Kronrod 1D/2D/3D/N-D quadrature, tanh-sinh, RK45/RK23/
DOP853/Radau/BDF ODE solvers, BVP solver), @code{optimize} (BFGS, L-BFGS-B,
CG, Newton-CG, Powell, Trust-Region Dogleg/NCG, SLSQP, Simplex LP, MILP, NNLS,
Dual Annealing, Differential Evolution, Basin-Hopping, SHGO, DIRECT, QAP),
@code{stats} (22 probability distributions, special functions, Quasi-Monte
Carlo Halton/Sobol/LHS/Poisson-disk, bootstrap/permutation resampling, 25+
hypothesis tests, KDE, PCA), @code{interpolate} (Cubic/Akima/PCHIP/B-Splines,
RBF, 2D/3D rectilinear & Delaunay griddata), @code{signal} (FIR/Butterworth/
Chebyshev/Elliptic/Bessel filters, SOS filtering, STFT/Welch/Lomb-Scargle/CZT,
LTI state-space systems), @code{sparse} (CSR/CSC/COO/DIA/BSR/DOK/LIL matrices,
CG/BiCGSTAB/GMRES/MINRES/LSQR/LU/ILU/ARPACK-style eigsh/svds, @code{csgraph}),
@code{spatial} (k-d tree, 2D Delaunay/Voronoi/Spherical Voronoi/Halfspace/
Polygon clipping, 3D @code{rotation} & @code{rigid_transform}), @code{cluster}
(k-Means++, hierarchical linkage, DBSCAN, OPTICS), and @code{autograd}
(forward-mode @code{dual_number} and reverse-mode Wengert computation
@code{tape} / @code{var}).

@node Tabular and Lazy Engine
@chapter Tabular and Lazy Engine
@cindex data_frame
@cindex lazy_frame

The @code{hyper_math::tabular} namespace unifies eager @code{series} /
@code{data_frame} manipulation (including @code{.str} regex/encoding/JSON and
@code{.dt} ISO-8601 temporal methods, dynamic temporal group-by, and
CSV/NDJSON/JSON/HTML/Markdown/LaTeX/@code{.hmb} I/O) with lazy query
optimization via @code{lazy_frame} and @code{sql_context}.

Pure C / FFI bindings are provided in @code{<hyper_math/hyper_math_c.h>}, and
the @code{hyper-math} command-line driver supports @code{--demo}, @code{--repl},
@code{--csv}, @code{--ndjson}, and @code{--eval}.

